2018 Pfizer Inc."},{"type":"Formula re: Contains","notes":"The centrum advantage\nThis superior formula combines the most clinically studied multivitamin brand, and a concentrated Omega-3, in one easy to swallow softgel.\n22 essential vitamins and minerals \n200 mg of Omega-3\n90% EPA + DHA concentration"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Designed to control fishy burps\nCentrum Multi + Omega-3 vs Men's 50+ Multivitamin Omega 3"},{"type":"FDA Disclaimer Statement","notes":"This statement has not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any disease."},{"type":"Formula re: Contains","notes":"22 Nutrients + Omega 3"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"All-in-one"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Advanced support for whole body benefits + heart, brain & eyes"},{"type":"FDA Statement of Identity","notes":"Multivitamin/Multimineral/Omega-3 Supplement"},{"type":"Formula re: Contains","notes":"Omega-3 fish oil\nOmega-3 may reduce the risk of coronary heart disease. Plus Vitamins B6, B12 and Folate for heart health\nHeart Health\nOmega-3 and 3 B-Vitamins plus magnesium for heart health. Vitamin C and E to support healthy circulation\nEnergy\nB-vitamins to help turn your food to energy for your day\nEye Health and Vision\nVitamins A, C, E and Omega-3 (DHA) to support your vision\nBrain Function\nOmega-3 (DHA), Zinc and B-vitamins - key nutrients to support your brain health\nMuscle Function\nMagnesium, Vitamins B6 and D - used by your body to support healthy muscles"},{"type":"Formula re: Contains","notes":"Includes 22 nutrients to support whole body health including B-vitamins to support heart health, zinc and B-vitamins to support normal brain function, and Vitamins A, C, and E to support eye health"},{"type":"Precautions re: Pregnant or Nursing or Prescription Medications","notes":"Not a replacement for cholesterol-lowering drugs."},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Supportive but not conclusive research shows that consumption of EPA and DHA Omega-3 fatty acids may reduce the risk of coronary heart disease."}],"targetGroups":["Seniors/Mature (>50 Years) - Men ONLY"],"thumbnail":"","upcSku":"","userGroups":[{"dailyValueTargetGroupName":"Adults and children 4 or more years of age","langualCode":"P0250","langualCodeDescription":"Adults and Children 4 years and above"}],"_source":"api"}